==Strategy==
This is a very simple stage, as tanky units that can survive many hits and keep going, like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Jamiera Cat]] shine greatly on this stage; if they are underlevelled however, the stage can become very difficult. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]] is also very useful against them, as usual. The Crazed Lizard Cats are the main threat of the stage. Stack tanky, hard-hitting units to deal with them quickly and blow up the enemy base before the Zackie Pengs spawn and ruin your incoming lines. Keep an eye on the Coffin Zoges while sending your heavy units out, and use Zombie Killers to protect them.

Alternatively, if you do not bring any [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]], you can continuously use the Coffin Zoges as stepping stones to hit the lizard cats with [[Wave Attack|waves]] or [[Long Distance]] attacks, since they can revive infinitely. This strategy will likely take a much longer amount of time, however, so you should do this only as a last resort. The Crazed Lizards give a very large amount of money when defeated. As the battle wears on, a Cat CPU may help matters greatly once the Crazed Lizards start to fall and the player's money is at a high amount.

After all the Doge Darks are dead a last resort option is to let them push to your base, get 3 Cyberpunks, wait until a perma slow chamber is formed, and stop sending units out. This will eventually snowball into an immense stack of Cyberpunks that can slowly but surely push back. While this will take a stupid amount of time, it is relatively effective. Just make sure you have a low-endurance rusher like Bahamut ready for if a Zackie Peng somehow breaks free. After a long enough (theoretically after 1 hour and 30 minutes,) you will have a Cyberstack able to kill the Crazed Lizards fast enough to push through to the base.

